<form class="form-horizontal">
  <h4>Camera</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Snapshot URL</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.snapshot_url">
      <span class="help-block">
        A single JPEG frame. OctoPrint fetches this, so 127.0.0.1 is correct.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Frames to average</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.frame_average">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Finding the camera</h4>
  <div class="alert">
    Nothing is remembered about where the camera is. Every run sweeps the bed
    for it. The X and Y below are where the active T0 nozzle last sat over the
    lens, for information. The Z is where the last focus sweep peaked, and the
    next one starts there.
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Last found X, Y, Z</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small" readonly
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.camera_x">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small" readonly
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.camera_y">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.camera_z">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bed sweep</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_row_mm">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.sweep_step_mm">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.search_z">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.closein_z">
      <span class="help-block">
        Row spacing in Y, step in X, the sweep height and the close-in
        height. At Z90 the camera sees about 75 by 47 mm, so rows 50 mm
        apart cannot miss the toolhead, and the toolhead is wider than the
        field, which is what the close-in needs.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bore ring span, step (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bed_search_span_mm">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.search_step_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        How far around the middle of the toolhead the run looks for the bore,
        at the working height.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Heights</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Floor (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.min_z">
      <span class="help-block">
        No move may go below this. The lens sits about 12 mm above the bed on
        the standard mount. Raise this if your mount is taller.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Safe Z (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.safe_z">
      <span class="help-block">Every travel move and every tool change happens at this height.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Focus sweep span, step (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_span_mm">
      <input type="number" step="0.25" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.focus_step_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        The run sweeps this far above and below the stored Z and stops where
        the bore is sharpest.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Home first</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="checkbox"
             data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.home_first">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Closed loop</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Probe distance (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.probe_distance">
      <span class="help-block">
        The known move used to measure the pixel scale and the camera rotation.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Backlash take-up (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.backlash_backoff_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        Every measured position is reached from the same direction, after
        overshooting by this much.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tolerance (mm), passes</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.001" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.tolerance_mm">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.max_passes">
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Bore detector</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Radii (px)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_core_r">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_inner_r">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_ring_lo">
      <input type="number" class="input-mini"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_ring_hi">
      <span class="help-block">
        Ignored centre, dark bore wall, then the bright collar from and to.
        Sized for about 75 px/mm. Check the red circle on the tab.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Minimum score</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_min_score">
      <input type="number" step="5" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.bore_track_score">
      <span class="help-block">
        For a first find, and for a bore already being followed.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Firmware guard</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Toolhead band centre X, Y</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.nominal_offset_x">
      <input type="number" step="0.01" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.nominal_offset_y">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Band half width (mm)</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.1" class="input-small"
             data-bind="value: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.offset_limit_mm">
      <span class="help-block">
        The Snapmaker toolhead throws away an offset outside 26 &plusmn; 1.2 mm
        in X, or 0 &plusmn; 1.2 mm in Y, and resets it to the default. The
        plugin refuses to send such a value.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Also send M500</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="checkbox"
             data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.nozzlealign.save_to_eeprom">
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
